cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ChimiaClaw: Rust-native signed artifact DAG for autonomous scientific agents"
message: >-
  If you use ChimiaClaw — including the MolADT canonical molecule substrate,
  the chem.dft.{request,result} schema, the orbital-density content-addressing
  pattern, or any of the signed-artifact worker boundaries — please cite this
  repository.
type: software
authors:
  - name: ChimiaDAO
    email: info@chimiadao.io
    website: "https://chimiadao.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xchemtina/ethglobal-openagents"
url: "https://github.com/xchemtina/ethglobal-openagents"
abstract: >-
  ChimiaClaw is a Rust-native runtime for autonomous scientific agents in
  which every action — chemistry computation, retrosynthesis, literature
  synthesis, procurement, governance vote, payment — is a signed,
  content-addressed artifact in a payload-bound DAG. The repository ships:
  a portable Molecular ADT substrate; an ORD→ADT bridge; a real PBE/def2-tzvp
  PySCF DFT path that signs chem.dft.result artifacts with HOMO/LUMO/total-
  density orbital cubes content-addressed via SHA-256; and feature-gated
  ENS / 0G / KeeperHub adapter surfaces. Built for the ETHGlobal "OpenAgents"
  hackathon track as a substrate for the future ChimiaDAO governance runtime.
keywords:
  - decentralized-science
  - rust
  - artifact-graph
  - dft
  - pyscf
  - chemistry
  - molecular-adt
  - ethereum
  - chimia-dao
